   <section class="jumbotron text-center">
      <div class="container">
         <h1 class="jumbotron-heading service_text_align">Keeping You Safe During COVID-19</h1>
         <h5 class="lead text-muted service_text_align">by Dr. Zhang | May 30, 2020 | News</h5>
         <br/>
         <p class="lead text-muted service_text_align">Bay Star Dental is happy to announce that as of June 1st, we are once again open for clinical appointments (cleanings, fillings, crowns, implants, extractions, etc.). </p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Please <a href="contact">contact us</a> to book your appointment. If you had an appointment scheduled during the shutdown, we’ll be in touch soon to get you back on the schedule.</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Patient safety has always been our top priority. We’ll continue to treat every patient with universal precautions and are taking extra measures to keep you and your family safe during this pandemic.</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Keep reading to learn more.</p>
         <br/>
         <h5 class="lead text-muted service_text_side_title">What we’re doing to keep you safe</h5>
         <br/>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Infection control has always been a top priority for our practice. In the midst of the current Coronavirus pandemic, we’d like to reassure you that our team continues to be committed to your health and well-being. </p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">We follow all recommendations made by the ADA, CDA, CDC, and San Mateo Department of Health. Our team is staying up-to-date on any new guidance issued by these agencies to ensure our procedures are current.
            We’re implementing extra precautions to exceed all mandated safety procedures, including:
         </p>
         <br/>
         <ol class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">
            <li>All areas of our office are fully sanitized before and after patient visits.</li>
            <li>Installing HEPA filter air purification units in our waiting room and in each patient room.</li>
            <li>Taking temperature of every team member before the day begins.</li>
            <li>Offering paperless forms online and in office with iPads, and online payment, so no more cross-contamination from using traditional papers, credit cards, checks and cash. </li>
            <li>Wearing the best-available personal protective equipment (PPE), including custom-fitted 3D-printed mask fitter, face shields, head caps and disposable gowns to prevent unknown cross-contamination.</li>
         </ol>
         <br/>
         <h5 class="lead text-muted service_text_side_title">What to expect at your next appointment</h5>
         <br/>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">In addition to the extra sterilization and infection control procedures above, you may notice a few changes at your next appointment.</p>
         <ol class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">
            <li>Our office will send out an online COVID-19 screening form before your appointment. You’ll be asked to fill out the same form again when you are in the office.</li>
            <li>Your appointments will be scheduled to allow for social distancing between patients (that might mean that you’re offered fewer options for scheduling your appointment).</li>
            <li>We’re doing our best to reduce waiting times for you and reduce the number of patients in the reception area at any one time.</li>
            <li>We proactively clean and disinfect our waiting rooms, patient rooms, and are limiting common “touch points,” like pens.</li>
            <li>Hand sanitizer will be available at check-in and check-out — we’ll encourage you to use it!</li>
            <li>Toys, books, magazines, and communal coffee bar amenities have been removed from our waiting rooms and patient rooms for infection control purposes.</li>
            <li>We request that families limit non-essential adults during office visits. When possible, only bring the child/children being seen for a visit with one parent/guardian.</li>
            <li>We require everyone entering the office to wear face masks. </li>
            <li>Patients experiencing a temperature, cough, or other COVID-19 symptoms will not be permitted in our office. Thank you for your understanding!</li>
         </ol>
         <br/>
         <h5 class="lead text-muted service_text_side_title">The importance of good oral hygiene during the pandemic</h5>
         <br/>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">While things may look a little bit different in our office right now, know that our dental team is committed to maintaining the quality of our care. We’ve missed seeing you here in our office and are ready to safely provide you with the high-quality, comprehensive care you’ve come to expect.</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">The importance of good oral hygiene during the pandemic</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Taking care of your dental health is always important — but it’s especially critical during this Coronavirus pandemic. There is a direct correlation to the health of the mouth and the overall body. Infection, inflammation, and other oral health issues have been linked to a variety of diseases.</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Don’t let oral health issues affect your ability to fight off a virus and stay healthy. Our team is here to keep your teeth and gums healthy, reducing your risk of getting sick and improving your health during this vulnerable time.</p>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">If you or a loved one is experiencing symptoms of fever or cough, we kindly ask you to reschedule your appointment to a later date by calling our office. We’re very flexible with rescheduled appointments as we understand everyone’s concerns at this time.</p>
         <br/>
         <h5 class="lead text-muted service_text_side_title">Thanks for your trust</h5>
         <br/>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">On behalf of the entire Bay Star Dental team, I would like to personally thank each and every one of you for trusting your dental care with us. We will get through these challenging times together. We look forward to continuing to provide you and your families with the best dental care in all of San Mateo.</p>
         <br/>
         <p class ="lead text-muted service_text_align">Dr. Xuyu Zhang/Dr. Allen Lee</p>
